Description: skip dh_doxygen invocation when nodoc is in DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-17
Bug-Athena: libyaml's debian/rules override_dh_installdocs-indep
 unconditionally calls dh_doxygen — but doxygen isn't installed in
 our build container (intentionally — DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc means
 we don't want to generate or ship API docs).  dh_doxygen errors
 with "Doxygen documentation not found" and the build dies.
 .
 Fix: guard the doxygen-driven docs step on the nodoc build option,
 matching the pattern Debian recommends for nodoc-aware rules.
 Behaviour without nodoc is unchanged (dh_doxygen runs as before).
 .
 TEMPORARY: nodoc is a workaround for missing doc-build tooling in
 the build pool, not a permanent policy.  DELETE THIS PATCH when
 CONF-08 lands and nodoc is dropped from [Source] BuildOptions /
 BuildProfiles in config/build.conf.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -6,8 +6,12 @@ export DEB_BUILD_MAINT_OPTIONS = hardening=+all
 	dh $@

 override_dh_auto_build-indep:
+ifeq (,$(findstring nodoc,$(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)))
 	$(MAKE) html
+endif

 override_dh_installdocs-indep:
 	dh_installdocs -i
+ifeq (,$(findstring nodoc,$(DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS)))
 	dh_doxygen -plibyaml-doc
+endif
